{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s46-p01",
      "text": "Laughter is a universal language for humans.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p02",
      "text": "It can help people to get on well with others.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p03",
      "text": "As children, we laugh when our parents make faces.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p04",
      "text": "Then we start to make others laugh like this.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p05",
      "text": "That's how we learn to play jokes.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p05.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p05.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p06",
      "text": "But is playing jokes only humans' ability?",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p07",
      "text": "Scientists believe that some animals also have the ability.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p08",
      "text": "Dogs are smart animals with a good nose.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p08.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p08.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p09",
      "text": "They often help people.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p10",
      "text": "But sometimes we see dogs play jokes on people.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p11",
      "text": "They come near slowly and then quickly run away.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p12",
      "text": "This act seems silly.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p13",
      "text": "But they may just want to have fun.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p14",
      "text": "When dogs are guarding, they sometimes hide behind a door to scare visitors in a playful way.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p15",
      "text": "They fool their owners too.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p15.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p16",
      "text": "But after a joke, they lick their owner, which is like giving a kiss to show they are friendly.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p16.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p16.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p17",
      "text": "Scientists say they have watched young apes play jokes.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p17.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p17.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p18",
      "text": "The young apes quietly follow adult apes and touch them secretly to surprise them.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p18.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p18.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p19",
      "text": "Then they playfully wait and watch what the adults would do.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p19.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p19.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p20",
      "text": "This action is similar to what human children do.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p20.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p20.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p21",
      "text": "Next time, when you find your pets doing something strange around you, maybe they are having jokes with you.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p21.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p21.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p22",
      "text": "So don't be mad if your dog borrows your shoe or your cat hides your sock.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p22.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p22.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s46-p23",
      "text": "They might just be trying to make you laugh.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p23.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s46-p23.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
